Subject: [PATCH 06863/11362] [outer-loop] ARC ka59 round-4: honest null, L7
 barrier-ram mechanic found

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on ka59 deepens round-3's L7 scouting.
Confirms the two rectangular e-framed helpers are active traversal tools
(6x3 passes three-row gaps, 3x6 passes three-column gaps) and finds a new
mechanic: a selected helper can RAM the other helper through an otherwise
solid barrier, recovering the vertical piece from the sealed central
chamber into its lower socket. Also finds a combined stack-launch-plus-ram
interaction crossing the color-15 partitions. Both helpers got socketed
and mapped but no L7 win observed -- a rendering glitch ended exploration
early with budget unused.

Honest null -- no fresh reproduce() gate run, no registry count change,
frontier stays at level 6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
